# No Collateral File Changes

Keep changes focused. Extra files or additional fixes are allowed when they are intentional and declared (in the PR description / commit body). Accidental noise is not.

## Rules

1. Stay focused, but declared extra work is fine. Note "also touched X because Y" rather than splitting or reverting genuine improvements.
2. Accidental import reordering by the IDE/formatter in files you did not intend to change should be reverted.
3. Before committing, review `git diff --name-only` and confirm every file is either part of the task or a declared extra. Restore accidental changes:
   ```bash
   git checkout HEAD -- <unintended-file>
   ```
4. Editing barrel files (`src/index.ts`) can trigger cascading import re-sorts in consumers - revert consumers that were not intentionally modified.
5. Whitespace-only / indentation-only diffs outside the task scope should be reverted unless they are an intentional, declared cleanup.

## Pre-Commit Checklist

- [ ] `git diff --name-only` lists only task files plus declared extras
- [ ] Any extra file / additional fix is noted
- [ ] No accidental import reordering or whitespace-only changes in unrelated files
- [ ] `npm run lint` and `npm run typecheck` pass
